# neuroTrade core rule

Read and follow @AGENTS.md before making changes. `AGENTS.md` is the shared rule set for Cursor and Codex.

For every non-trivial task:
- Read @docs/00_INDEX.md and the subsystem docs relevant to the requested work.
- Inspect the existing implementation before editing.
- Keep the change limited to the approved phase/concern.
- If the change would alter locked architecture, strategy/risk semantics, execution behavior, schema/API contracts, or add a new dependency/integration not already approved, stop and present the decision for approval first.
- Never default to live trading. `PAPER` is the safe default.
- Never commit or print secrets.
- Never let Strategy/AI bypass deterministic Risk and Execution boundaries.
- Never blindly retry an ambiguous order submission; reconcile first.
- Run relevant lint/typecheck/tests and report exact results.
- Update architecture/API/behavior docs in the same change when contracts change.
